  "caveats": [
    "Current rates are 2025 final adopted rates \u2014 the newest complete set the state publishes. 2026 rates are not certified until after the August hearings.",
    "Eagle Mountain's tentative schedule (read May 26) implied a rate of 0.001842 and a 245% increase. The rate the city is actually proposing is 0.001700, a 220.9% increase measured against the newer certified rate. The charts use 0.001700.",
    "Percent increases are the figures on each city's Truth-in-Taxation notice: the proposed rate measured against that city's certified rate. They are not increases in your total tax bill, and they are not the ratio of proposed collections to current collections — for Eagle Mountain that ratio is 245%, against a noticed 220.9%.",
    "Highland's and Orem's proposals raise a dedicated levy (library; public safety), not the general city rate.",
    "Draper and Bluffdale levy in Utah County but lie mostly in Salt Lake County.",
    "Resulting rates are each city's current rate plus the rate increase implied by its own published figures (the dollar rise on its stated average home, over 55% of that home's value). This avoids assuming the noticed percentage applies to the general city rate \u2014 for Highland and Orem it does not. Tested against Eagle Mountain, the only city publishing a proposed rate, the method reproduces 0.001700. Rows marked \u2021 rest on a rounded dollar figure and are approximate."
  ],
